t Center】\nL160:   * 【19†Viewpoint Blog†viewpoints.dji.com】\nL161:   * 【20†Announcements】\nL162:   * 【21†Media Coverage】\nL163:   * 【22†Insights】\nL164: \nL165: ### DJI News\nL166: \nL167: # DJI Advances Action Camera Industry with Osmo Action 5 Pro’s Revolutionary Image Quality\nL168: ## DJI delivers action camera with industry-first professional features, including a groundbreaking 13.5-stop for both an exceptional high dynamic range and excellent low-light performance\nL169: \nL170: 2024-09-19\nL171: \nL172: Send to Email\nL173: \nL174: Copy Link\nL175: \nL176: Link Copied\nL177: September 19 – DJI, the global leader in civilian drones and creative camera technology, today unveils the Osmo Action 5 Pro. The latest generation of DJI’s popular Osmo action camera series delivers several industry-first features rivaling professional cameras.\nL178: From the 13.5-stop dynamic range and 4-hour battery life to the built-in subject centering and tracking, the Osmo Action 5 Pro sets a new quality standard for action photography, capturing every adventure from the sea to the mountains, whether in the sun or the snow.\nL179: \"By combining the image quality of a professional camera with the rugged durability of an action camera, we continue to innovate and set new standards for the industry,” said Paul Pan, Senior Product Line Manager at DJI. “Creators have evolved, becoming more sophisticated in the stories they tell and the moments that they capture. Instead of making incremental improvements, we strive to push the entire action camera category forward and evolve with these creators.”\nL180: 13.5-stops of dynamic range deliver groundbreaking image quality\nL181: Osmo Action 5 Pro features a next-gen 1/1.3” sensor with a 2.4 μm pixel size and a high dynamic range of up to 13.5 stops, making it the first action camera with specs that rival professional cameras. Images can be captured in 10-bit D-Log M and support hybrid log-gamma (HLG) high-brightness displays. It can also shoot high-dynamic, low-light video at 4K/60fps, capturing intricate shadow details without overexposing highlights, thereby enhancing overall image quality.\nL182: Additionally, SuperNight mode with AI noise reduction algorithms can overcome the darkness in extremely low-light environments to yield cleaner and clearer footage.\nL183: \nL184: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDJI - The World Leader in Camera Drones/Quadcopters for Aerial Photography (https://www.dji.com/pr/newsroom/news/dji-release-osmo-360-us)\nciteturn5view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dji.com/pr/newsroom/news/dji-release-osmo-360-us\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 0\nThis page has no readable lines.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFujifilm announces affordable XC 35mm F2 prime lens | DPReview (https://www.dpreview.com/news/4262945623/fujifilm-announces-more-affordable-xc-35mm-f2-prime-lens/)\nciteturn5view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dpreview.com/news/4262945623/fujifilm-announces-more-affordable-xc-35mm-f2-prime-lens/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 168\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†BETA】\nL3: \nL4:   * 【2†NEWS】\nL5:   * 【3†REVIEWS】\nL6:   * 【4†BUYING GUIDES】\nL7:   * 【5†CAMERAS & LENSES】\nL8:   * 【6†FORUMS】\nL9: \nL10:   * 【7†COMPARE】\nL11:   * 【8†GALLERIES】\nL12: \nL13: 【9†Sign In】 【10†Register】 [Button: Sign out ]\nL14: \nL15: 【9†Sign In】 【10†Register】 [Button: Sign Out ]\nL16: \nL17: [Input: Search www.dpreview.com]\nL18: \nL19: Popular Searches\nL20: \nL21:   * 【11†sony rx100 vii】\nL22:   * 【12†leica d-lux 8】\nL23:   * 【13†sony a7 v】\nL24: # Fujifilm announces affordable XC 35mm F2 prime lens\nL25: \nL26: The ‘XC’ variant uses the same optical design as the existing XF 35mm F2, but has no aperture ring and a plastic mount to lower the cost.\nL27: \nL28: 【14†274274 Comments】\nL29: \nL30: 【15†Image: the dpreview logo against a black background】\nL31: \nL32: By 【16†DPReview Staff】\nL33: \nL34: Published January 23, 2020\nL35: \nL36: ·\nL37: \nL38: See more of our coverage in your search results\nL39: \nL40: When you use DPReview links to buy products, the site may earn a commission.\nL41: Alongside the X-T200, Fujifilm has announced the Fujinon XC 35mm F2 lens. For those of you not familiar with Fujifilm’s lens names, the ‘XC’ denotes the company’s more affordable optics.\nL42: \nL43: The XC 35mm F2 should pair nicely with Fujifilm’s lower-cost models, such as the X-T200 and X-T30\nL44: The XC 35mm F2 is essentially a rehoused version of the XF 35mm F2 R WR. It has a plastic mount and less-solid-feeling construction, and features neither an aperture ring nor weather sealing (the ‘R’ and ‘WR’ in the XF version’s name, respectively). However, it does feature the same optics as the XF version, so image quality should be comparable.\nL45: The difference is that this brings the XC down to a price of $199. The result is a much more affordable 50mm-equivalent lens for newcomers wanting to expand their photography with a prime lens. In this sense, it’s like the ‘nifty fifty’ lenses traditionally available for most DSLR systems, but in a focal length nicely suited to APS-C users.\nL46: ### Press Statement\nL47: \nL48: [From Fujifilm’s X-T200 Press Release]\nL49: For those interested in expanding their X-T200 tool kit, the new FUJINON XC35mmF2 lens gives an equivalent to 52mm field of view on 35mm format. Weighing just 130g and measuring 46.5mm in length, this new prime lens has nine elements, including two aspherical lens elements in six groups, which work to produce sharp and crisp images with creamy bokeh.\nL50: AF operation is quick and near silent thanks to the use of an internal focus system and a stepping motor, which is used to drive the focusing elements quickly and accurately.\nL51: XC35mmF2 lens: $199 USD ($259.99 CAD)\nL52: \nL53: Want to stay up to date on the latest product news and releases? Add DPReview as a preferred source to ensure our independent journalism makes it to the top of your Google search results.\nL54: \nL55: [Button: View 274 comments ]\nL56: \nL57: Comments 【17†Forum View】\nL58: ### Related Topics\nL59: \nL60: 【18†fujifilm】, 【19†lens-news】\nL61: \nL62: ### More from fujifilm\nL63: \nL64: 【20†Image: A coral-colored Instax Square 2 instant camera held in a hand.】\nL65: \nL66: 【18†fujifilm】\nL67: \nL68: ### 【21†Fujifilm Instax Square 2 review: simple doesn’t always mean easy】\nL69: \nL70: 【22†Image: A three quarter shot of the EOS R8 II with the RF 45mm F1.2 STM lens.】\nL71: ### 【23†Canon EOS R8 II review: new design, major fixes but frustrations remain】\nL72: \nL73: 【24†Image: Black-and-white tunnel with a bright exit and silhouetted people walking along a central ramp.】\nL74: \nL75: 【25†community】\nL76: \nL77: ### 【26†From a Kodak Brownie: one photographer’s decades-long journey through cameras】\nL78: \nL79: 【27†Image: Black Tamron 16-50mm camera lens with ribbed zoom rings on a gray surface.】\nL80: \nL81: 【28†lenses】\nL82: ### 【29†Tamron’s 16-50mm F2.8 is a fast, sub-$550 kit lens replacement for every APS-C system】\nL83: \nL84: 【30†Image: three different cameras arranged in a collage】\nL85: \nL86: 【31†camera】\nL87: \nL88: ### 【32†The best cameras for travel in late 2026】\nL89: \nL90: 【33†Image: Purple and pink chive flowers with a bumblebee on a purple bloom.】\nL91: \nL92: 【34†throwback-thursday】\nL93: \nL94: ### 【35†Throwback Thursday: Sigma APO 50-150mm F2.8 EX II】\nL95: ### Topics\nL96: \nL97:   * 【36†Beginner tips†tag】\nL98:   * 【37†Cameras】\nL99:   * 【38†Lenses】\nL100:   * 【38†News】\nL101:   * 【39†Photography】\nL102:   * 【40†Sample images】\nL103:   * 【41†Technology】\nL104:   * 【42†Videos】\nL105: \nL106: ### Editorial Content\nL107: \nL108:   * 【43†Articles & insights】\nL109:   * 【44†Buying guides】\nL110:   * 【45†Event coverage】\n