r X-A2\nL25: \nL26: Fujifilm has announced two zoom lenses which will be bundled with the new X-A2. The Fujinon XC16-50mm II F3.5-5.6 offers a 24-76mm equivalent range and has a closer minimum focusing distance than its predecessor. The XC50-230mm II F4.5-6.7 OIS provides a 76-350mm equivalent range on APS-C and improved image stabilization. Read more.\nL27: \nL28: 【14†2828 Comments】\nL29: \nL30: 【15†Image: the dpreview logo against a black background】\nL31: By 【16†DPReview Staff】\nL32: \nL33: Published January 15, 2015\nL34: \nL35: ·\nL36: \nL37: See more of our coverage in your search results\nL38: \nL39: When you use DPReview links to buy products, the site may earn a commission.\nL40: Fujifilm has announced two zoom lenses which will be bundled with the new X-A2 in one or dual lens kits. The Fujinon XC16-50mm II F3.5-5.6 offers a 24-76mm equivalent range and has a closer minimum focusing distance than its predecessor (30/40cm down to 15/35cm). According to Fujifilm, it features an updated design and better performance.\nL41: The XC50-230mm II F4.5-6.7 OIS provides a 76-350mm equivalent range on APS-C and offers improved image stabilization compared to the Mark I model (now 3.5 stops vs 3.0 stops). Fuji says that both lenses offer better build quality and smoother operation.\nL42: No word on whether these lens will be available separately.\nL43: \nL44: * * *\nL45: \nL46: Press release:\nL47: ## FUJIFILM ANNOUNCES NEW SELFIE-READY X-A2 CSC AND PREMIUM COMPACT XQ2\nL48: \nL49: Two new versatile zoom lenses, XC16-50mm II and XC50-230mm II, also added to give users wide range of photographic possibilities\nL50: Valhalla, N.Y., January 15, 2015 – FUJIFILM North America Corporation today announced the new FUJIFILM X-A2 compact system camera (CSC), an ultra-light, selfie-ready camera that gives users quick access to a 175° tilting LCD with face and eye detection for fast and fun pictures.\nL51: The X-A2 is an affordable entry point into the X-Series line of digital cameras and delivers outstanding image quality using its large 16.3 Megapixel APS-C CMOS sensor, easy operation and wireless image transfer for quick photo sharing.\nL52: Also new to the X-Series line is the FUJIFILM XQ2, a premium pocket-sized digital camera with a bright FUJINON F1.8 4x zoom lens, an advanced 12 Megapixel 2/3” X-Trans CMOS II sensor with phase detection, and the EXR Processor II that delivers the fastest autofocus speed in its category of up to 0.06 seconds.\nL53: FUJIFILM X-A2 faces forward for incredible shots\nL54: The FUJIFILM X-A2 ships with the newly-developed FUJINON XC16-50mm II (24-76mm) F3.5-5.6 OIS zoom lens and has a 175° tilting LCD with face and eye detection for candid and fun selfies. The X-A2 also features optical image stabilization of approximately 3.5-stops, making it easier to take telephoto and low light images.\nL55: The X-A2 uses a newly-developed Eye auto focus (AF), Auto Macro AF and Multi-Target AF to achieve easy and accurate auto focus performance, bringing premium image quality and performance of the X-Series to everyone.\nL56: The XC16-50mm II is a versatile lens that is ideal for a wide range of photographic subjects, including clear low-light scenes, beautiful portraits and vibrant landscapes. The lens consists of 12 all glass elements in 10 groups including 3 aspherical elements and 1 ED element. The lens features seven round-edged aperture blades, which offer 17 stops in 1/3 EV increments for precise aperture control.\nL57: FUJINON XC50-230mm II (76-350mm) F4.5-6.7 OIS\nL58: Also new to pair with the X-A2 is the improved FUJINON XC50-230mm II (76-350mm) F4.5-6.7 OIS lens that adds even more versatility by offering an expanded zoom range that delivers consistently outstanding optical performance throughout. The XC50-230mm II uses optical image stabilization to ensure superb performance and effectively reduces blur when shooting at longer focal lengths and in low light.\nL59: FUJIFILM XQ2 makes performance easier to carry\nL60: The FUJIFILM XQ2 uses the 12 Megapixel 2/3” X-Trans CMOS II sensor that is designed to control moiré and false color generation by using an original color filter array with a highly randomized pixel arrangement. This technology removes the need for an Optical Low Pass Filter (OLPF) that degrades resolution.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntroducing XF8mmF3.5 R WR | News | FUJIFILM X Series & GFX - Singapore (https://www.fujifilm-x.com/en-sg/news/introducing-xf8mmf3-5-r-wr/)\nciteturn5view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.fujifilm-x.com/en-sg/news/introducing-xf8mmf3-5-r-wr/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 402\nL0: 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†PRODUCTS】\nL3: \nL4: [Button: Back] PRODUCTS\nL5:     * 【2†Browse】\nL6:       * 【1†Cameras】\nL7:       * 【3†Lenses】\nL8:       * 【4†Accessories】\nL9:       * 【5†Software】\nL10:     * 【2†By System】\nL11:       * 【6†GFX Series】\nL12:         * 【7†Cameras】\nL13:         * 【8†Lenses】\nL14:       * 【9†X Series】\nL15:         * 【10†Cameras】\nL16:         * 【11†Lenses】\nL17:     * 【2†Group Items ( Link disabled )】\nL18:       * 【2†Compare】\nL19:         * 【12†Cameras】\nL20:       * 【2†About Our Technology】\nL21:         * 【13†Filmmaking】\nL22:         * 【14†Film Simulation】\nL23:         * 【15†X-Trans CMOS】\nL24:     * 【2†B2B Customers】\nL25:       * 【16†Digital Imaging Solution】\nL26:       * 【17†IR Camera】\nL27:       * 【18†Camera Control SDK】\nL28: [Button: Back] GFX Series 【6†View all】\nL29: \nL30: Cameras Mirrorless Digital Camera\nL31:     * 【19†GFX100 II】\nL32:     * 【20†GFX100S II】\nL33: Fixed Lens Camera\nL34:     * 【21†GFX100RF】\nL35: Filmmaking Camera\nL36:     * 【22†GFX ETERNA 55】\nL37: \nL38: [Button: Back] GFX Series 【6†View all】\nL39: Lenses Pevné ohniská\nL40:     * 【23†GF23mmF4 R LM WR】\nL41:     * 【24†GF30mmF3.5 R WR】\nL42:     * 【25†GF45mmF2.8 R WR】\nL43:   